# Node identity — NEVER build this into an image.
#
# `identity/` holds the node's federation key material: the sealed classical
# blobs (`<alias>.ed25519.seed.blob` + `.master.key`) and the bare ML-DSA-65
# PQC seed. Building from a working checkout was copying ALL of it in — on this
# tree, 63 sealed blobs, 63 master keys and 2 PQC seeds, ~540 KB of accumulated
# identities from every boot the checkout has ever had.
#
# Two consequences, and the second is the serious one:
#   1. The research container inherits identities it must not have, and then
#      fails in exactly the way the isolated harness exists to prevent.
#   2. Private key material leaves the host inside an image layer, where it
#      persists in the build cache and in anything the image is pushed to.
#
# A container must mint its own identity. There is no case where copying in a
# host's is correct, so this is an unconditional exclusion, not a convenience.
identity/

